    "body": "Speaking with one of the authors for the RFC (J. Alakuijala), I have confirmed that the changes to the spec during transition to RFC are editorial in nature and should not require work by clients to handle any format changes. Apparently the last substantive change to the algorithm was a bug fix in 2014. Whether we want this to be class 2 or 3 is still an open question, but it seems like from a technical perspective, this is just updating the location of the spec, so it seems like class 2 is appropriate.",
